    "status": "present",
    "value": "Swaps never change which rows are equal or complementary, so a solvable grid has exactly two row types that are bitwise complements, and the same for columns. That is equivalent to every rectangle corner XOR board[0][0]^board[i][0]^board[0][j]^board[i][j] being 0. The first row must also have a balanced count of ones (n/2 for even n, floor or ceil of n/2 for odd n), and so must the first column. Once feasible, rows and columns are solved independently: count positions where the first row disagrees with the pattern 1010..., and each swap fixes two misplaced positions. For even n take the cheaper of the two target patterns; for odd n only the pattern with an even misplaced count is reachable."
  },
